{"id": "EUVD-2026-103505", "enisaUuid": "7ac84b33-ab6d-31e4-bc22-e9ee13726e69", "description": "libstrophe through 0.14.0 contains a stack-based buffer overflow vulnerability in SCRAM_Hi that allows malicious XMPP servers to overflow a 128-byte stack buffer by sending an oversized SCRAM salt. Attackers can send a server-first-message whose s= attribute decodes to more than 124 bytes, aborting the client or overwriting stack memory in NDEBUG builds.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:38:04", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libstrophe-scram-salt-stack-overflow", "https://github.com/strophe/libstrophe/blob/0.14.0/src/scram.c", "https://github.com/strophe/libstrophe/blob/0.14.0/src/sasl.c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libstrophe-through-0.14.0-stack-based-buffer-overflow-via-scram-salt-in-scram-hi"], "aliases": ["GHSA-37wj-432m-6r6f", "CVE-2026-112063"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d71a0e09-dc19-3ade-a737-1945f9ea2040", "product": {"name": "libstrophe", "vendor": {"name": "strophe"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.14.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "11abf66b-ce1b-3e44-a30d-83bc67d23d88", "vendor": {"name": "strophe"}}], "isExploited": false}